{# Advance notice for the Auth0 -> native sign-in migration (issue #147): a strip
   at the very top of the sticky header, above the topbar. Same look as the older
   .competition-panel-info pattern (primary background, white text, 12px).

   The header is `position: sticky`, so it takes its own space in the flow and
   this strip can be any height - one line in English on a desktop, three in
   German on a phone - without anything below it needing to know. Overlays that
   have to sit under the header follow `--header-height`, which is measured from
   the real element (see assets/controllers/header_height_controller.js).

   Dismissed per browser via localStorage, never per user: this rides on pages
   that are shared-cacheable for anonymous visitors (#164), so reading or writing
   a session here would put a cookie on every page. The inline script in
   base.html.twig hides it before first paint for anyone who dismissed it, so it
   never flashes in and never shifts the page. #}
<div class="sign-in-changes-notice" data-controller="sign-in-changes-notice">
    <div class="container">
        <span>{{ 'sign_in_changes.notice.text'|trans }}</span>
        {# Phones get the headline only - the strip has to stay a strip. The rest,
           and the explainer behind the link, carry the detail from tablet up. #}
        <span class="d-none d-md-inline">{{ 'sign_in_changes.notice.text_extra'|trans }}</span>
        <a href="{{ path('sign_in_changes') }}">{{ 'sign_in_changes.notice.link'|trans }}</a>
        <button
            type="button"
            class="sign-in-changes-notice-close"
            aria-label="{{ 'sign_in_changes.notice.dismiss'|trans }}"
            data-action="sign-in-changes-notice#dismiss"
        >&times;</button>
    </div>
</div>
